message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "bioinfo05: Compartment-specific transcriptomic convergence between OA and OP - RNA splicing programme axis"
abstract: >-
  Multi-omics, hypothesis-free discovery project on osteoarthritis (OA)-osteoporosis (OP)
  comorbidity. Core finding: transcriptomic convergence between OA and OP is
  compartment-specific (mesenchymal versus haematopoietic), not disease-specific.
  OA cartilage and OP bone-marrow mesenchymal stem cells share a concordant
  down-regulation of the RNA splicing machinery (49 core splicing factors),
  whereas circulating monocytes follow an independent, partly opposite trajectory.
  Analysis integrates three complementary null models (pathway-label permutation
  conditional on marginal significance, within-cohort case-control permutation,
  and gene-set family clustering) across seven public cohorts (303 samples).
